# Action Creators (actions.ts)

## Context

`app/src/actions.ts` holds the sanctioned action creators (`addTask`,
`toggleTask`, `removeTask`, `setFilter`, `setPriority`) — the only place
action objects are constructed. UI/component code calls these helpers instead
of building `{ type, payload }` literals by hand, so the payload shape for
each `Action` variant stays defined in exactly one place.

## Rule

- Every `Action` variant in `app/src/types.ts` must have exactly one
  corresponding creator function here, named after the action's intent (e.g.
  `addTask` for `"task/added"`), returning the literal `Action` object.
- A creator's parameters must map 1:1 to its action's `payload` fields — no
  extra parameters, no repackaging into a different shape.
- Do not construct `Action` object literals anywhere else in `app/src`
  (components, reducer callers, tests excluded) — always call the creator.
- When adding a new `Action` variant, add its creator here in the same change,
  keeping the existing named-export, one-function-per-action style.

## How to verify

1. Every member of the `Action` union in `app/src/types.ts` has a matching
   exported function in `app/src/actions.ts`.
2. `grep -rn "type: \"" app/src --include=*.ts \| grep -v "actions.ts\|reducer.ts\|types.ts\|.test.ts"` —
   should find zero matches (no hand-built action literals outside the
   sanctioned files).
3. `cd app && npm test` stays green.
